- net
- pass
- door
- mesa_foot

' This is the desk of the foot. Here the foot makes each signature that a
' world makes with a secret, but not the signatures of the pages of that
' world. The foot makes a signature when a record asks for it. A hand or a
' door writes an ask and does not hold a key.
'
' An ask is a record below /<self>/io/mesa/ask that tells what is wanted
' (want) and that is still not marked done. The foot answers each ask one
' time, in one event. That event writes what the ask asked for and marks the
' ask done (1) with what the foot tells the ask. Or the event marks the ask
' done (2) with the reason why not.
'
' The foot has three secrets. It keeps them as its files and not as records:
' - the live seed that signs pages
' - the custody seed that signs the identity log of this world
' - a maker secret
'
' The secret of each invitation that this world mints comes from the maker
' secret. The custody seed of each name that this world claims also comes from
' the maker secret. Thus the two files are all that it is necessary to keep
' safe.
'
' The foot makes the signatures before it asks the world to write. What the
' foot gives to the world holds statements, letters and grants, and these are
' public. It holds no secret.
+ desk
  + keys
    : live=nat custody=nat maker=nat
  + tag
    ' This function gives a number or a word as bytes.
    \ text=nat
    ^ nat
    | add text (bex (mul 8 (wid text)))
  + invitation
    ' This function gives the secret of the invitation that this world mints
    ' under a number. The foot derives this secret each time it is necessary
    ' and does not write it.
    \ k=desk/keys id=nat
    ^ nat
    | Blake3Keyed (Blake3Keyed k.maker (desk/tag "invite")) (desk/tag id)
  + claimed
    ' This function gives the custody seed that this world holds for a name
    ' that it claimed.
    \ k=desk/keys name=nat
    ^ nat
    | Blake3Keyed (Blake3Keyed k.maker (desk/tag "claimed")) (desk/tag name)
  + custody
    ' This function gives the custody seed that this world signs with for a
    ' name. The name is the name of this world or a name that this world
    ' claimed.
    \ k=desk/keys me=nat name=nat
    ^ nat
    ? (eq name me) k.custody
    | desk/claimed k name
  + root
    ' This function gives the place where the world keeps asks.
    \ self=iota
    ^ path
    [self 'io 'mesa 'ask]
  + pending
    ' This function gives the asks that still have no answer from the foot.
    \ self=iota state=namespace
    ^ row[[at=path ask=myth]]
    = none=row[[at=path ask=myth]] []
      root (desk/root self)
    | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (gt record.nat_at(['done] 0) 0) acc
      ? (eq 0 record.txt_at(['want]).len) acc
      | acc.snoc([root.weld(rel) record])
  + used
    ' This function gives the asks that are answered and that got a secret
    ' that is still there. For each of these asks, it gives the number that
    ' the ask got the secret under.
    \ self=iota state=namespace
    ^ row[[at=path handed=nat]]
    = none=row[[at=path handed=nat]] []
      root (desk/root self)
    | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (eq 0 record.nat_at(['done] 0)) acc
      ? (eq 0 record.nat_at(['handed] 0)) acc
      ? (gt record.nat_at(['spent] 0) 0) acc
      | acc.snoc([root.weld(rel) record.nat_at(['handed] 0)])
  + mark
    ' This function marks an ask as answered, with what the foot tells the
    ' ask.
    \ at=path told=myth
    ^ [p=path q=writ]
    [at (writ/poke told.put(['done] (pails/n 1)))]
  + say
    ' This function gives a turn that asks the world for these writes as one
    ' event.
    \ writes=row[[p=path q=writ]] foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 (mesa_foot/bid (mesa_foot/order/write writes)))]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + refuse
    ' This function puts a mark on an ask that the foot cannot answer. Then
    ' the foot does not try that ask again.
    \ at=path why=str foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = told=myth (myth/sing ['done] (pails/n 2)).put(['why] (pails/t why))
      writes=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[at (writ/poke told)]]
    | desk/say writes foot
  + mint
    ' This function mints an invitation: a name that is not claimed. The name
    ' is founded on a custody key made from a secret that this world derives
    ' under the number of the ask (id). The function keeps the card of the
    ' name with the founding and the first statement of the name. The first
    ' statement gives the live key to this world until the name is claimed.
    ' The function tells the name to the ask. dat is what the founding binds.
    \ k=desk/keys at=path ask=myth foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = id ask.nat_at(['id] 0)
    ? (eq 0 id) (desk/refuse at "an invitation needs a number" foot)
    = made (pass/mint (desk/invitation k id) ask.nat_at(['dat] 0) (Ed25519PublicKey k.live))
      card=path [foot.self 'io 'mesa ($x made.name)]
      log=row[pass/statement] [made.first]
      told (desk/mark at (myth/sing ['name] (pails/n made.name)))
      only=row[[p=path q=writ]] [told]
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 (mesa_foot/errand (mesa_foot/order/meet card made.made log) only))]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + claim
    ' This function does the first act of the person that opens an invitation.
    ' The act is one statement, signed with the secret of the invitation. The
    ' statement moves the custody of the name to a key of this world, and it
    ' names the live key of this world. secret is what the door of this world
    ' got. It comes to the foot as a file and is not a record.
    \ k=desk/keys secret=nat at=path ask=myth state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = name ask.nat_at(['name] 0)
    ? (lt (wid secret) 2) (desk/refuse at "the invitation's secret was not handed over" foot)
    ? (eq 0 name) (desk/refuse at "a claim names what it claims" foot)
    ? (eq name (mesa_foot/id foot.self)) (desk/claim_self k secret at ask state foot)
    | desk/claim_name k secret name at ask foot
  + claim_self
    ' This function is for a world that was prepared for a place and that
    ' claims itself. Custody becomes the custody seed of that world, and the
    ' world takes the claim onto its own card. If the ask names a session and
    ' when the session stops, the same event lets that session in. It does
    ' this under a grant that the new custody signs. This is because the
    ' person that proved the secret of the invitation is the person that the
    ' world was prepared for. And until this claim, the world let no person
    ' in.
    \ k=desk/keys secret=nat at=path ask=myth state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = home (mesa_foot/home foot)
      name (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
      session ask.nat_at(['session] 0)
      until ask.nat_at(['until] 0)
    ?> (./some stands) (pass/held home (net/sees state)) (desk/refuse at "this world has no log to claim" foot)
    = s (pass/claim secret name stands (Ed25519PublicKey k.custody) (Ed25519PublicKey k.live))
    ? (either/is_err (pass/next name stands s)) (desk/refuse at "the secret is not this invitation's" foot)
    = told (desk/mark at myth/new)
      g (pass/allow k.custody name session until)
      entry=[p=path q=writ] [(door/at foot.self session) (writ/make (door/grant g))]
      alone=row[[p=path q=writ]] [told]
      both=row[[p=path q=writ]] [told entry]
      with (? ((eq 0 session) || (eq 0 until)) alone both)
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 (mesa_foot/errand (mesa_foot/order/turn home s) with))]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + claim_name
    ' This function is for a world that claims a name that is not its name.
    ' The world keeps the log of the name on a card. The founding (form,
    ' custody, dat) and the first statement (first, as it travels) come with
    ' the ask. The function examines them against the name before it signs.
    ' Custody becomes a key that this world derives for the name.
    \ k=desk/keys secret=nat name=nat at=path ask=myth foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = made (pass/founding ask.nat_at(['form] 0) ask.nat_at(['custody] 0) ask.nat_at(['dat] 0))
      card=path [foot.self 'io 'mesa ($x name)]
    ?> (./some first) (pass/got ask.nat_at(['first] 0)) (desk/refuse at "a claim needs the name's first statement" foot)
    = one=row[pass/statement] [first]
    ?> (./ok stands) (pass/read name made one) (desk/refuse at "the founding and first statement are not this name's" foot)
    = s (pass/claim secret name stands (Ed25519PublicKey (desk/claimed k name)) (Ed25519PublicKey k.live))
    ? (either/is_err (pass/next name stands s)) (desk/refuse at "the secret is not this invitation's" foot)
    = log=row[pass/statement] [first s]
      told (desk/mark at myth/new)
      only=row[[p=path q=writ]] [told]
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 (mesa_foot/errand (mesa_foot/order/meet card made log) only))]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + bring
    ' This function lets a name (by) bring this world before another world
    ' (to), at an address. If the ask names none, the name (by) is this world.
    ' If not, it is an invitation that this world claimed. The custody that
    ' this world holds for that name signs the introduction, and the custody
    ' of this world signs it too. This world keeps the introduction on its
    ' card for the other world, in the slot bring. From there, the foot says
    ' it on each tick.
    \ k=desk/keys at=path ask=myth state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = me (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
      home (mesa_foot/home foot)
      to ask.nat_at(['to] 0)
      by (? (eq 0 ask.nat_at(['by] 0)) me ask.nat_at(['by] 0))
      port ask.nat_at(['port] 0)
      peer=path [foot.self 'io 'mesa ($x to)]
    ? (eq 0 to) (desk/refuse at "an introduction is to a world" foot)
    ? (eq 0 port) (desk/refuse at "an introduction says where the world is reached" foot)
    ?> (./some made) (pass/founded home (net/sees state)) (desk/refuse at "this world has no founding" foot)
    ?> (./some stands) (pass/held home (net/sees state)) (desk/refuse at "this world has stated no key" foot)
    ? !(net/live peer (net/sees state)) (desk/refuse at "this world keeps no card for that world" foot)
    = letter (pass/letter (pass/introduce (desk/custody k me by) k.custody to by me made stands ask.txt_at(['host]) port))
      writes=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[peer (writ/poke (myth/sing ['bring] (pails/n letter)))] (desk/mark at myth/new)]
    | desk/say writes foot
  + grant
    ' This function makes a grant: permission to act at a door, for a session.
    ' The custody that this world holds for the name signs the grant. If the
    ' ask names none, the name is the name of this world. The function tells
    ' the grant to the ask. The session is the hash of a secret that this
    ' world does not see.
    \ k=desk/keys at=path ask=myth foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = me (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
      name (? (eq 0 ask.nat_at(['name] 0)) me ask.nat_at(['name] 0))
      session ask.nat_at(['session] 0)
      until ask.nat_at(['until] 0)
    ? (eq 0 session) (desk/refuse at "a grant is for a session" foot)
    ? (eq 0 until) (desk/refuse at "a grant ends" foot)
    = g (pass/allow (desk/custody k me name) name session until)
      told (desk/mark at (myth/sing ['sig] (pails/n g.sig)).put(['name] (pails/n name)))
      writes=row[[p=path q=writ]] [told]
    | desk/say writes foot
  + link
    ' This function is for the secret of an invitation. The secret is for the
    ' person that will get the link of the invitation. The function does not
    ' tell the secret to the ask. The foot puts the secret as a file in
    ' io/mesa/out, under the number of the invitation. The door of this world
    ' takes the secret from there one time. Here, the function only marks the
    ' ask.
    \ at=path ask=myth foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    ? (eq 0 ask.nat_at(['id] 0)) (desk/refuse at "a link is to an invitation's number" foot)
    = writes=row[[p=path q=writ]] [(desk/mark at myth/new)]
    | desk/say writes foot
  + year
    ' This function gives the time, in seconds, that the first session of a
    ' world continues.
    ^ nat
    31536000
  + doorless
    ' This function tells if this world keeps no grant at all. If it keeps
    ' none, the world let no person in.
    \ self=iota state=namespace
    ^ bool
    = kept=path [self 'io 'door]
    | eq 0 (sovereign_peek kept state).tap.len
  + own
    ' This function tells if the custody seed of this world is the custody
    ' that its card states, or if its card states none. A world prepared under
    ' the key of an invitation is not its own until it is claimed. It has no
    ' door until then.
    \ k=desk/keys state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ bool
    = stated (net/held ['custody] (mesa_foot/home foot) (net/sees state))
    ? (eq 0 stated) .true
    | eq stated (Ed25519PublicKey k.custody)
  + first
    ' This function makes the first session of a world: a grant for a new
    ' secret. The foot made that secret and put it, as text, in one of its
    ' files, for the person at the machine. That person is the owner because
    ' that person is at the machine. The custody seed of this world signs the
    ' grant. If the card of the world still states no custody, the function
    ' states the key there. Thus the door has a key to examine a grant
    ' against.
    \ k=desk/keys token=str now=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = me (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
      home (mesa_foot/home foot)
      stated (net/held ['custody] home (net/sees state))
      mine (Ed25519PublicKey k.custody)
      session (door/named token)
      g (pass/allow k.custody me session (add now desk/year))
      grant=[p=path q=writ] [(door/at foot.self session) (writ/make (door/grant g))]
      states=[p=path q=writ] [home (writ/poke (myth/sing ['custody] (pails/n mine)))]
      alone=row[[p=path q=writ]] [grant]
      both=row[[p=path q=writ]] [grant states]
    ? !(desk/own k state foot) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    ? (eq 0 stated) (desk/say both foot)
    | desk/say alone foot
  + founded
    ' This function is for a world that a host started under a name. The host
    ' that prepared the world put one line of text in a file of the foot
    ' (pass/birth). That line gives the founding and the first statement of
    ' the name. The function examines them against the name of the world and
    ' keeps them on the world's own card. The first statement names the key
    ' that runs the world at this time and a custody that is not the custody
    ' of this world. Thus the world is not its own, and lets no person in,
    ' until it is claimed.
    \ text=str foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = home (mesa_foot/home foot)
    ?> (./some found) (pass/birth_of text) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = [made first] found
      log=row[pass/statement] [first]
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 (mesa_foot/bid (mesa_foot/order/meet home made log)))]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + answer
    ' This function answers one ask. secret is what the ask got, or no value.
    \ k=desk/keys secret=nat at=path ask=myth state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = want ask.txt_at(['want])
    ? (equal[str] want "mint") (desk/mint k at ask foot)
    ? (equal[str] want "claim") (desk/claim k secret at ask state foot)
    ? (equal[str] want "bring") (desk/bring k at ask state foot)
    ? (equal[str] want "grant") (desk/grant k at ask foot)
    ? (equal[str] want "link") (desk/link at ask foot)
    | desk/refuse at "the desk does not know this ask" foot
